Nightglass star positions are a subset of the HYG catalog, version 4.4,
compiled by David Nash (astronexus). That catalog is licensed under
Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

The subset keeps stars of visual magnitude 5.0 and brighter, plus a few
fainter stars needed to complete a stick figure. Positions are mean places
from the catalog. Proper names included here follow the names carried in
that catalog.

Constellation stick figures in sky/data/figures.json are traditional
patterns written as pairs of catalog stars. They are recorded as
astronomical facts, not copied from a chart or a software transcription.

Faint figure drawings in sky/data/art/ are taken from Sidney Hall's
Urania's Mirror (1825), a public-domain set of constellation cards.
The scans live on Wikimedia Commons. Each file here is one figure,
with the paper cleared so the engraved lines read as light marks, and
anchored to catalog stars so the figure follows the sky. The card,
artist, year, and Commons page for each figure are listed in
sky/data/art/credits.json.

Short notes in sky/data/constellations.json are original summaries of
the 88 constellations: names, meanings, area order, and a sentence or
two of background. They are not copied from an encyclopedia article.

Planet, Moon, and Sun positions are computed with astronomy-engine by
Don Cross, vendored at sky/vendor/astronomy.browser.min.js under the
MIT license. The license text is in sky/vendor/LICENSE.
